Description:
At Dandelion Renewables we strive to deliver the best quality, the best system reliability and excellence in customer service. Your first initial free consultation will help you make the decision if renewable energy and feasibility studies are a right fit for you personally or professionally.

We specialize in delivering the following services:

- feasibility study for solar, wind or energy-efficiency;
- roof-top and ground mounted solar panels installation;
- wind power systems installation;
- wind turbines service and maintenance;
- grid-tie and off-grid projects design;
- meteorological tower lease;
- energy audits and electric load management;
- municipal and regulatory applications;
- advocacy for renewable and distributed generation.

Dandelion Renewables ensures that every installation becomes a positive experience for you, your family, your business and your neighbours. We are confident that by sharing and spreading this positive experience around, together we can make the world a better and a cleaner place to live.

The Canadian Green Bank initiative is being sponsored by Canadian Green Fund Inc. (CGFI), which is a federally incorporated clean energy and sustainability investment fund solely focused on projects within Canada. We welcome opportunities to invest in First Nations projects.

The Canadian Green Fund is singularly focused on delivering unique funding solutions that provide positive social, environmental and financial results for all. We use funds from a variety of financing sources to back green projects on flexible commercial terms and mobilize other private sector capital into Canada’s green economy. 

Some of the elements of our business model are as follows: 
•	we are an active investor in Canadian based green infrastructure projects; 
•	we are primarily focused on investing in four broad sectors: energy efficiency; renewable energy generation; energy storage and conservation; and, waste water treatment solutions.

Our investments are conservatively managed while dynamically driven to help fund the creation of new energy and conservation infrastructure across the Canada and with that, new jobs in construction, manufacturing, logistics and operations. 

By demonstrating that projects can be both green and profitable - as well as socially responsible - we can mobilize the required capital to accelerate the movement to a greener and more sustainable economy in Canada. Rather than 'crowding out' capital of any type we work to 'crowd in' capital from a variety of sources. CGFI is inclusive not exclusive. 

•	investments must make positive returns that are measured against our social (jobs), environmental and financial mandates that are inline with a project's risk; 
•	we assist developers by working on a blended portfolio rate of return basis; 

We provide an opportunity for well-considered projects to obtain the necessary financing and assistance to create successful projects that will drive the Canadian Economy forward.

É possível conciliar crescimento econômico – e o consequente aumento da demanda por energia – com sustentabilidade ambiental?

Após 27 anos de experiência no mercado de energia elétrica, a Vector criou a Vector Solar, uma empresa que tem em seu DNA a resposta:Sim, é possível! Não apenas possível, mas esta será a tônica do novo século. A Vector Solar está pronta para atender seus clientes garantindo qualidade, economia e sustentabilidade ambiental.

Missão:

Oferecer soluções integradas e completas de sistemas fotovoltaicos e LED para residências, empresas e entidades públicas.

Valores:

    Dedicação ao sucesso do sistema fotovoltaico;
    Oferecer o estado da arte da energia solar fotovoltaica;
    Confiança e responsabilidade pessoal em todos os relacionamentos.

Visão:

    Participar pró-ativamente do desenvolvimento do mercado solar fotovoltaico brasileiro;
    Ser reconhecida pela excelência e competitividade nos serviços prestados;
    Fomentar parcerias com Centros de Pesquisa e Desenvolvimento;
    Estar sempre em sintonia com a crescente busca de soluções sustentáveis.

Vision Statement - “We are a leader in environmentally responsible waste management programs and services.”
Mission Statement - “To provide environmentally responsible, non-hazardous waste management services for our municipal members, our residents and businesses
Guiding Principles -
•	Continue to meet or exceed environmental standards required to be leaders in waste management;
•	Maximize beneficial reuse of waste;
•	Educate the public on environmentally sound waste management practices;
•	Strike a balance between strategic economic risk and successful business operations;
•	Explore responsible expansion and marketing opportunities. 
•	Be an employer of Choice

L'OBV Scabric est un organisme à but non lucratif incorporé en 1993 qui est voué à l’amélioration de la qualité de l’eau et des sols des bassins de la Zone Châteauguay. 

Nos secteurs d’intervention :

• Diffusion d’informations et éducation; 
• Concertation avec les différents secteurs d’activités du territoire; 
• Sensibilisation du public et des intervenants du milieu à l’approche par bassin versant; 
• Restauration, conservation, mise en valeur et protection des berges, des habitats et des milieux humides;
• Suivi des dossiers régionaux, transfrontaliers et nationaux en environnement.
